1	// Acceptance tests for the change request:
2	//   "Make sure that discount shows up everywhere I check what is owed. That means the invoice, the
3	//    statement and the home screen."
4	//
5	// An invoice can already carry a PERCENTAGE discount (seed field `discountPct`, Flyway V27). Its own
6	// detail page already breaks the money into subtotal / discount / final total (invoice-discount.spec
7	// .ts, invoice-summary). But the three places that answer "how much is OWED" have been ignoring the
8	// discount and billing the full, undiscounted amount:
9	//   - the INVOICE's own amount-still-to-pay       -> invoice-due-amount
10	//     (how much is left on this invoice after its payments — invoice-due-amount.spec.ts)
11	//   - the client's STATEMENT                       -> statement-invoice-due (per row) and
12	//     client-outstanding-total (client-statement.spec.ts)
13	//   - the HOME SCREEN                              -> dashboard-outstanding-total
14	//     (the dashboard is the home screen — dashboard.spec.ts; the money still owed across everything)
15	//
16	// After this change, every one of those owed figures must be worked out from the DISCOUNTED total
17	// (the subtotal with the percentage taken off), not the full amount. "Owed" keeps its established
18	// meaning everywhere else: an invoice's due is its (now discounted) total minus what has been paid on
19	// it; the statement's total is the sum of its rows' dues; the home screen's total counts only invoices
20	// actually SENT (DRAFT/PAID excluded — invoice-owed-sent-only.spec.ts). This change only puts the
21	// discount into the money math; it does not change which invoices count.
22	//
23	// Asserts ONLY through the UI (data-testid). Data is arranged via resetAndSeed, which honours
24	// invoices { id, projectId, amount, status, discountPct } and payments { id, invoiceId, amount, date }
25	// (alongside clients / projects). An explicit `amount` is the invoice's subtotal (TestSupportController
26	// takes it as the undiscounted figure); `discountPct` is the percentage taken off it. This change adds
27	// NO new audit record, so nothing is asserted through the audit channel.
28	//
29	// Money values are matched the way their sibling specs match these same anchors: invoice-due-amount
30	// and the statement figures leniently (a leading "$" and a trailing ".00" both optional), the
31	// dashboard total in the app's exact money format. Amounts, percentages and payments are chosen so the
32	// correct (discounted) owed figure is never a substring of the WRONG (undiscounted) one a pre-change
33	// implementation produces, nor of any other figure on the page. This test SHOULD FAIL before the
34	// change: today all three owed figures ignore the discount and show the full amount.
35	import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';
